WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.640
 Hate crimes against religious minorities have become increasingly common in India.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:10.980
 Report after report have highlighted the rise of violent incidents against the

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:16.400
 minorities in India. The recent data shows that among the minorities hate crimes

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:22.480
 against Muslims have the largest volume with a 300% increase since right-wing

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:28.380
 government came to power in the center in 2014. One of them is Jamiat Ulama-i-Hind

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:33.080
 Hind, the oldest and largest socio-cultural organization of Indian

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:38.560
 Muslims, which has been on the ground for long, combating hate crimes committed

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:44.480
 against the country's religious minorities. And in this struggle, their

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.400
 justice and empowerment initiative hopes to change the disturbing trends of the

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:53.320
 increasing hate crimes against religious minorities. With the mission of

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.680
 safeguarding their human rights and countering hate speech targeted against

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.720
 them, JEM aims to ensure the implementation of equal rights, justice,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:08.240
 peace, religious tolerance and coexistence for all in the country. Their

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.920
 objectives include developing a hate crime database, promoting the rule of

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:18.360
 law and access to justice, upholding citizens security and human rights,

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:23.560
 defending religious minorities and marginalized communities and promoting

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:28.520
 peace-building and interfaith harmony. These objectives tie with our ultimate

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:33.240
 goal of empowering the oppressed and wrongly persecuted and promoting a more

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:37.960
 just and inclusive society in India. For all of this to come together, JEM has

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:43.640
 four departments - Hate Crime Response Unit, Case Review Committee, Media Unit and

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:51.080
 Legal Unit. And this is how our work channels through them. It begins with the

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:56.160
 organization's reporting and ground networks when news about hate crimes is

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:01.520
 first received. We believe in verifying cases ourselves rather than relying

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:09.560
 solely on secondary sources. For this second step, local members of our Hate

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:14.600
 Crime Response Unit are deployed on the ground to provide immediate aid and

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:21.880
 collect testimonies from the victims. We also have our own website, a form to

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:27.800
 report a hate crime and a helpline number. All the received and collected

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:33.800
 information is then verified, analyzed and further listed under one of the seven

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:40.520
 types of cases that we are equipped to handle, namely acts of hate, acts of

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:47.680
 violence, attacks on religious places, police atrocities, discrimination,

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:54.600
 exclusion and prejudice, state-sponsored discriminatory practices and media

00:02:54.600 --> 00:03:01.880
 manipulation and distortion of facts. At JEM, a specialized case review committee

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:07.240
 carefully screens these cases to assess how to help with our limited resources.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:14.840
 And this is the final and most crucial part, intervention, which can fall into

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:23.080
 either of the four umbrella categories - reporting, documentation, advocacy and

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:31.680
 training and capacity building. With our diligent reporting, we bring forth policy

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:36.640
 demands, appeal to figureheads and dignitaries by writing letters and grab

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:43.760
 the media spotlight on these otherwise ignored issues. With facts out there, we

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:50.440
 continue with meticulous documentation of each and every case. We maintain a hate

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:55.160
 crime database, which documents alarming trends of hate crimes and

00:03:55.160 --> 00:04:00.440
 simultaneously aids in developing tailored solutions to combat these crimes.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:06.760
 In this regard, we also publish four quarterly reviews and an annual review every

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:13.120
 year. All of this documentation offers evidence for our long-term strategy for

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:18.560
 intervention, which is our advocacy for better legislation and policy making at

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:23.440
 different levels. Some of our legally advocated interventions have had a

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:30.000
 significant positive impact on the outcome of cases. At JEM, we also believe

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.480
 in capacity-building and empowering people. For this, we aim to establish state,

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:43.360
 city and town units in as many locations as possible. Well-versed in social

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:49.000
 political dynamics, these units are trained to promptly identify and address

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:55.280
 hate crimes and build trust and solidarity between different communities.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:05:00.440
 They play a critical role in countering hate crimes by providing local

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:05.560
 presence, immediate assistance to victims and connecting them with legal and

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:11.360
 victim assistance services. Through their tireless efforts, JEM works towards

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:16.960
 empowering victims, promoting equality and fostering peace in India. Community

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:21.440
 support is crucial in the endeavor to counter hate crimes and promote a more

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:27.120
 inclusive society. Together, we can stand against discrimination and violence,

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:32.680
 ensuring that every individual feels safe and protected, regardless of their

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:37.400
 religious or social background. By supporting organizations like JEM and

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:42.240
 actively participating in initiatives, promoting dialogue, understanding and

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:47.960
 harmony, we can create a society where tolerance and acceptance prevail. Let us

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:53.560
 join hands and become champions for justice, equality and peace, supporting

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:57.440
 the good fight against hate.

